6) docker-compose down
#It will remove all the containers and network created by docker-compose up -d

7) docker-compose down -v
#It will remove volume from host as well,along with removing all the containers and network created by docker-compose up -d

8) #To enter inside conatiner,
docker exec -it ec2-user_mongodb_1 mongosh
#Note entering in mongosh shell


Note: if I am using any docker command like docker exec -it <cname> mongosh, it will work
But if I am using docker-compose command like docker-compose exec -it ec2-user_mongodb_1 mongosh, it wont work. For docker-compose, you have to give name of service which you have defined in compose.yaml and not container name
So it will be  docker-compose exec -it <nameofService> mongosh

9) To pass a file name to docker compose.So lets say I have multiple docker-compose files. So from which one to make containers?
docker compose -f my-custom-file.yml up -d

10) Authenticate to mongodb container for listing/creating databses/collection etc.

 docker-compose exec -it <svcName> mongosh -u <username> -p <password>

11) to call one service from other, docker Compose gives us the DNS name based on the service name

<protocol>://<service>:<port>
